{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh: decide whether the reason for revert a106e0e still stands. This is the one piece of genuinely open work left in my unclaimed queue, and it is blocked on a judgement rather than on effort.\n\nWHAT IS AT STAKE. Request b5edb0eb asks to re-integrate the instance-identity and review-independence work codex approved at d38ccd8a. Half of it is already in main and I verified that rather than assuming it: IndependenceIndependent and IndependenceSelfReview appear across internal/workroom, and resolveReviewed and reviewBasis are in fold.go. I have exercised that half repeatedly — every verdict I ratified in the last day carried independence \"independent\", and the fold resolved each named artifact through resolveReviewed.\n\nWHAT IS ABSENT FROM MAIN. Distinct instance identities, seeded-operator refusal, and actor-retire custody on effective verdict only. Grepping internal/ for instanceID, seededOperator and actorRetire finds nothing outside tests. Two names b5edb0eb's own premise says main carries, standingArtifact and liveArtifact, are also absent, so part of its stated basis no longer holds.\n\nWHY IT NEEDS YOU AND NOT ME. d38ccd8a is an ancestor of main, but its content was deliberately removed: merge 9ecdb07 combined divergent ancestry and a106e0e reverted that merge back to the 5a5220e tree, for a stated reason, under request 42357253. Reviving it means judging whether that reason still holds. That is a decision about a deliberate revert, and implementing it because a row exists would be treating my own past filing as authorization — b5edb0eb is mine, addressed to myself, which AGENTS.md says self-initiated work should never have produced.\n\nTHE THREE OPTIONS AS I SEE THEM, and I have no stake in which you pick.\n  (a) The revert's reason still stands. Then the remainder should not be revived, and b5edb0eb should be retired as decided-against rather than left looking like open work.\n  (b) The reason no longer holds. Then a real request